<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Umayyad invasion of Gaul</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">719–759</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Umayyad invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> was the series of campaigns launched from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> into Frankish territory after 719, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narbonne">Narbonne</a> was taken. Raids reached deep into Aquitaine and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-al-ghafiqi">Abd al-Rahman al-Ghafiqi</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a> in 732. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short">Pepin the Short</a> later recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimania">Septimania</a>, taking Narbonne in 759 and ending Muslim rule north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/umayyad-invasion-of-gaul.jpg" alt="Umayyad invasion of Gaul" width="320" height="313" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unochepassava94 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umayyad_invasion_of_Gaul-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
